name: Telecom re-rating (tariff validation)
tagline: "Independent re-rating of rated usage against an effective-dated tariff - tariff-table hygiene, ambiguity verdicts and an unbilled preview, over a synthetic corpus"
description: "A re-rating / tariff-validation content pack (slices R0 and R1 of the plan: tariff versioning and ambiguity only). Two feeds - the rated usage a billing system produced, and the tariff as one row per version with its own effective dates and an optional PRIORITY - and two chained sql.template Jobs. rr_tariff_hygiene judges the tariff table itself (rows in force at once with the same rate or different rates, gaps, negative or missing rates, inverted intervals) and rr_rerate re-rates each call at its start, giving one verdict per call (single, agree, precedence, disagree, none), an expected charge or an expected RANGE, and separate under-charged and over-billed amounts that never net. A call that an ambiguous tariff could justify is explained, not leakage. It explains no cause yet, groups no root cause, compares nothing with the invoice and raises no Alert: those arrive in the next slices. Every threshold is configuration. This pack is an unbilled preview: it is not priced or ordered yet. Needs the Standard, Advanced or Preview edition."
minEdition: standard
icon: heroicons_outline:calculator
contents[6]: "2 Pipelines + schemas (rated usage, tariff versions)", "2 chained sql.template Jobs (tariff hygiene, re-rating)", "4 Datasets (2 feeds, 2 Job-written)", "Zero-row schema seeds", "Runbook skeleton", "Example SLA policies and Escalation Rules (inert)"
